DEFENDANT META PLATFORMS, INC.’S RESPONSE IN OPPOSITION TO
PLAINTIFF’S MOTION FOR REFERRAL TO AN EARLY SETTLEMENT
CONFERENCE
Defendant Meta Platforms, Inc., (“Meta”) by and through its undersigned counsel, hereby
respectfully opposes Plaintiff Marvelle J. Ballentine’s Motion for Referral to an Early Settlement
Conference. (Dkt. No. 133). In support, Meta fully adopts the arguments in NCMEC’s response in
opposition to Plaintiff’s motion (“NCMEC’s Opposition”), which explains why “a settlement
conference is highly unlikely to be productive” or “a justifiable expenditure of the resources of
this Court or the Parties.” Dkt. No. 136 at 1. As explained in NCMEC’s Opposition, Plaintiff’s
only supported justification for an early settlement conference—“the number and scope of the
pending proceedings” (Dkt. No. 133 at 2)—was caused exclusively by Plaintiff, who has filed
nearly 25 motions in this matter, including 11 motions over a two-day period.
For the foregoing reasons, Meta respectfully requests that the Court deny Plaintiff’s Motion
for Referral to an Early Settlement.
